data.content:
Here's the component:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Renders a `<ul>` with each item plus Move Up/Down buttons. Uses `@key` for efficient diffing and disables buttons at the boundaries.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — Key design points:

- **Generic** (`TItem`) — works with any item type.
- **Immutable input** — `Items` parameter is `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`, copied to a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutated).
- **`ItemTemplate`** — typed `RenderFragment<TItem>` so consumers get `@context`.
- **`OnOrderChanged`** — fires an `EventCallback` with a read-only snapshot of the reordered list after each swap.

Usage matches your example:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { /* ... */ };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
